+
+**English Translation:**
+From behind the bridge,
+the oldest bridge —
+how many thousand times have you risen over it...
+and... how many thousand lovers
+sighed at the sight of you?...
+and... how many thousand eyes
+repeated the lines of light,
+from tear to river water?...
+The Zayandeh-rud...
+O ancient wayfarer,
+O witness of the bridge's youth, lantern of lovers,
+O moon...
+great moon...
+full moon...
+a greeting from behind the bridge...
+with the one old tree,
+from the foot of the bridge... salaam.
